/* =====================================================================
   Common Variable Immunodeficiency (CVID) — QSP Mechanistic Map
   보통 가변 면역결핍증 · 일차 항체결핍증 (Primary Antibody Deficiency)
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE ORGANISING IDEA

     CVID IS TWO DISEASES SHARING ONE LABORATORY DEFINITION,
     AND ONLY ONE OF THEM IS TREATED BY THE TREATMENT WE GIVE.

   Every CVID patient meets the same criterion: IgG below two standard
   deviations for age, with low IgA and/or IgM, impaired vaccine
   response, and no other explanation. From that single definition two
   almost unrelated illnesses emerge:

     DISEASE 1  INFECTION  — recurrent sinopulmonary infection with
                encapsulated bacteria. It is caused by the missing
                antibody, it is quantitatively predictable from the
                serum IgG trough, and immunoglobulin replacement
                very largely FIXES it.

     DISEASE 2  IMMUNE DYSREGULATION — autoimmune cytopenias, GLILD,
                enteropathy, granuloma, polyclonal lymphoproliferation,
                lymphoma. It occurs in roughly 20-30% of patients, it
                is a T-cell and tolerance disorder rather than an
                antibody deficiency, immunoglobulin replacement does
                essentially NOTHING for it, and it is what kills people.
                Resnick's 4-decade cohort: non-infectious complications
                raised mortality roughly 11-fold; infection alone,
                once replaced, barely moved it.

   A model of CVID that only models the antibody is a model of the
   part of the disease that is already solved. This map therefore runs
   the two arms in PARALLEL from a shared genetic and cellular root,
   lets each drug act on exactly one arm, and forces the model to
   reproduce the fact that maximal IgG replacement leaves GLILD
   untouched — a deliberate structural NULL, not an assertion.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE THIRD THING: STRUCTURE IS AN INTEGRAL, AND INTEGRALS DO NOT
   COME BACK

   Between the two arms and the clinical endpoints sits a third layer
   that neither drug reverses: IRREVERSIBLE STRUCTURAL DAMAGE.
   Bronchiectasis is the archetype. Each pneumonia deposits a small
   permanent increment of airway wall destruction; destroyed airway
   clears mucus badly; badly cleared airway is colonised; colonised
   airway infects more often. That is a POSITIVE FEEDBACK LOOP with an
   irreversible state variable inside it — a ratchet.

   The ratchet is why the single most important number in CVID is not
   a dose. It is the DIAGNOSTIC DELAY, historically 4-7 years from
   first symptom. Two patients on identical replacement, identical
   trough, identical everything, differ permanently in FEV1 according
   to how long the ratchet ran before anyone measured an IgG. The map
   draws the delay explicitly (cluster 20) because the model's job is
   to price it.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   WHAT THE EXPOSURE-RESPONSE ACTUALLY SAYS, AND WHERE IT IS ABUSED

   Orange's 2010 meta-regression of 17 IVIG studies is the quantitative
   backbone of this entire field: pneumonia incidence falls about 27%
   for every 100 mg/dL increase in IgG trough. That number is solid.
   The corollary usually quoted alongside it — that the fitted line
   reaches ZERO pneumonia at a trough of about 1400 mg/dL — is an
   artefact of fitting a straight line to a ratio. This model keeps
   the 27%-per-100 mg/dL slope and implements it as an EXPONENTIAL, so
   protection improves without ever becoming sterile. The difference
   is not cosmetic: the linear form says "titrate to 1400 and stop
   worrying", the exponential says "there is a diminishing-returns
   knee near 800-1000 and above it you are buying very little".
   The map draws both readouts so the model can be asked which fits.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE FOUR TRADE-OFFS THE MAP IS BUILT TO EXPOSE

     1. ROUTE / INTERVAL vs TROUGH.  Trough is not set by the monthly
        dose alone but by how the dose is spread. IVIG q4w produces a
        600-800 mg/dL peak-to-trough sawtooth; weekly SCIG at the same
        AUC is nearly flat and therefore has a HIGHER trough from the
        same monthly milligrams. If protection tracks trough, smoothing
        the profile is free efficacy. This must FALL OUT of the PK, not
        be asserted — hence the explicit depot, lymphatic uptake,
        FcRn recycling and saturable catabolism nodes.

     2. IMMUNOSUPPRESSION vs INFECTION.  Arm 2 needs rituximab,
        azathioprine, abatacept or sirolimus. All of them raise
        infection risk. But here is the CVID-specific asymmetry the
        map is drawn to reveal: rituximab's usual major cost in other
        diseases is secondary hypogammaglobulinaemia — and in CVID
        that cost is already PAID and already REPLACED. Rituximab is
        therefore comparatively cheap in CVID, and its real price is
        cellular, not humoral. The BAFF node matters here: depleting
        the B-cell sink drives soluble BAFF up, which is why B cells
        return skewed.

     3. SPLENECTOMY vs SEPSIS.  Refractory ITP historically led to
        splenectomy. In an asplenic patient with no opsonising
        antibody of their own, the encapsulated-organism hazard is
        multiplicative, not additive.

     4. TROUGH TARGET vs "BIOLOGIC IgG LEVEL".  Bonagura's point is
        that the dose that stops infections is patient-specific and
        can be far above any population target. The map carries both a
        FIXED-TARGET and a TREAT-TO-EFFECT strategy node so the model
        can simulate the two policies against a population with
        variability in BOTH clearance and intrinsic infection
        susceptibility.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   Legend
     box / ellipse       biological species, state or process
     hexagon             drug or intervention
     octagon             clinical endpoint or patient-reported outcome
     diamond             measurement / laboratory readout
     doubleoctagon       irreversible state (does not return)
     house               genetic lesion
     solid arrow         activation / increase
     T-bar (tee)         inhibition / decrease
     dashed              slow, transcriptional, plastic or years-scale
     bold red            the bronchiectasis ratchet (vicious circle)
     blue                pharmacological intervention
     purple              immune-dysregulation arm (arm 2)
     orange              adverse effect / therapeutic cost
   ===================================================================== */

digraph CVID_QSP {
  graph [rankdir=TB, newrank=true, splines=spline, overlap=false, nodesep=0.20,
         ranksep=0.58, fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=11,
         labelloc="t", compound=true, bgcolor="white",
         label=<<b>Common Variable Immunodeficiency (CVID) — 보통 가변 면역결핍증</b><br/>
                <font point-size="12">QSP mechanistic map · ARM 1 antibody deficiency (replaceable) ∥ ARM 2 immune dysregulation (not replaceable) → irreversible structure</font>>];
  node  [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=9, style="filled", penwidth=0.9];
  edge  [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=8, arrowsize=0.6, penwidth=0.9, color="#555555"];

  /* ================================================================
     1. GENETIC AND MOLECULAR SUBSTRATE
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_gene {
    label="1 · 유전적 기반 (Genetic Substrate) — 단일유전자 원인은 2-30%, 나머지는 다인성";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#8D6E63"; fillcolor="#EFEBE9"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=house, fillcolor="#D7CCC8", color="#8D6E63"];

    G_TACI    [label="TNFRSF13B (TACI)\nC104R / A181E\n8-10% of CVID, but also\n1-2% of healthy — a MODIFIER,\nnot a cause"];
    G_BAFFR   [label="TNFRSF13C (BAFF-R)\nP21R homozygous\nnaive B-cell survival failure"];
    G_CTLA4   [label="CTLA4 haploinsufficiency\n(CHAI) — penetrance ~60-70%\n→ Treg suppression failure"];
    G_LRBA    [label="LRBA deficiency (LATAIE)\nCTLA-4 lysosomal degradation\n→ loss of surface CTLA-4"];
    G_NFKB1   [label="NFKB1 haploinsufficiency\nmost common monogenic\ncause in adult CVID cohorts"];
    G_NFKB2   [label="NFKB2 (DAVID syndrome)\nhypogammaglobulinaemia +\nACTH deficiency"];
    G_PIK3CD  [label="PIK3CD GOF / PIK3R1 LOF\nAPDS 1 / APDS 2\n→ hyperactive PI3Kδ-AKT-mTOR"];
    G_ICOS    [label="ICOS deficiency\nTfh help failure\n(first CVID gene, 2003)"];
    G_CD19    [label="CD19 / CD81 / CR2(CD21)\nBCR co-receptor complex\ndefects"];
    G_TWEAK   [label="TNFSF12 (TWEAK)\nheterozygous — impaired\nTNF-family co-signalling"];
    G_IKZF1   [label="IKZF1 (IKAROS)\nhaploinsufficiency —\nprogressive B-cell loss"];
    G_ARHGEF1 [label="ARHGEF1, TNFRSF13B modifiers,\nATP6AP1, RAC2, SEC61A1,\nMOGS, TRNT1 …"];
    G_POLY    [label="다인성 기여\nPolygenic burden, HLA-DR/DQ,\nCNV load, epigenetic\nCSR-locus methylation"];
    G_SOMATIC [label="체성 모자이시즘\nSomatic mosaicism\n(late-onset phenocopies,\ne.g. NFKB1, VEXAS overlap)"];
    G_YIELD   [label="유전 진단 수율\nMonogenic yield: 2-10% in\nunselected adults, 15-30% if\nearly onset / dysregulation /\nconsanguinity"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     2. B-CELL DEVELOPMENT AND THE CLASS-SWITCH BLOCK
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_bcell {
    label="2 · B세포 발달과 계열전환 차단 (B-cell Development & the Class-switch Block)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#1565C0"; fillcolor="#E3F2FD"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#BBDEFB", color="#1565C0"];

    B_PROB    [label="골수 pro-B / pre-B\nBone marrow output\n— NORMAL in CVID\n(the block is PERIPHERAL)"];
    B_IMM     [label="미성숙 B세포\nImmature B (CD10+)"];
    B_TRANS   [label="전이기 B세포\nTransitional B\nCD38hi IgMhi\n(expanded in Freiburg Ia)"];
    B_NAIVE   [label="나이브 B세포\nNaive B (CD27− IgD+)\n— usually preserved"];
    B_ACT     [label="활성화 B세포\nActivated B cell\nBCR + CD40 + cytokine"];
    B_GC      [label="생식중심 B세포\nGerminal centre B\n(dark zone ↔ light zone)\n— dysmorphic GCs in CVID"];
    B_AID     [label="AID / UNG\n계열전환 재조합 (CSR)\n— the rate-limiting step"];
    B_SHM     [label="체세포 과돌연변이\nSomatic hypermutation\n(affinity maturation)"];
    B_MEM     [label="전환 기억 B세포\nSwitched memory B\nCD27+ IgD− IgM−\n★ THE core CVID deficit"];
    B_MEMIGM  [label="IgM 기억 B세포\nIgM memory (CD27+IgD+IgM+)\n— marginal-zone-like,\nanti-polysaccharide"];
    B_CD21LO  [label="CD21low B세포 확장\nCD21low B expansion\n>10% → splenomegaly,\nautoimmunity, granuloma"];
    B_PBLAST  [label="형질세포 전구체\nPlasmablast\n(CD38hi CD27hi)"];
    B_PCSHORT [label="단수명 형질세포\nShort-lived plasma cell\n(spleen, lymph node)"];
    B_PCLONG  [label="장수명 형질세포\nLong-lived plasma cell\n(bone marrow niche)\n— source of residual IgG"];
    B_ANERGY  [label="B세포 무반응성\nBCR anergy / defective\nCa2+ flux and NF-κB"];
    B_EURO    [label="EUROclass 분류\nsmB− vs smB+ ×\nCD21low ×  transitional\n→ phenotype prediction"];
    B_FREIB   [label="Freiburg 분류\nIa (CD21low>20%) / Ib / II\n— Ia = splenomegaly,\ngranuloma"];
    B_LAMINA  [label="점막 형질세포 부재\nAbsent plasma cells in\ngut lamina propria\n— near-pathognomonic"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     3. BAFF / APRIL / TACI / BCMA AXIS
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_baff {
    label="3 · BAFF/APRIL 축 (BAFF-APRIL Axis) — B세포 생존 신호와 sink 소실";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#00838F"; fillcolor="#E0F7FA"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=box, fillcolor="#B2EBF2", color="#00838F"];

    A_BAFF    [label="가용성 BAFF\nSoluble BAFF (BLyS)\n— ELEVATED in CVID\nbecause the B-cell SINK\nis reduced"];
    A_APRIL   [label="APRIL (TNFSF13)\nplasma-cell survival,\nT-independent CSR to IgA"];
    A_BAFFR   [label="BAFF-R (BR3)\nnaive B survival"];
    A_TACI    [label="TACI (TNFRSF13B)\nT-independent CSR,\nnegative regulation of\nB-cell expansion"];
    A_BCMA    [label="BCMA (TNFRSF17)\nplasma-cell survival"];
    A_SBCMA   [label="가용성 BCMA\nsBCMA — decoy sink,\ntracks plasma-cell mass"];
    A_TRAF    [label="TRAF2/3 → NIK →\nNF-κB2 (p52) processing\ncanonical + non-canonical"];
    A_SINK    [label="B세포 sink 소실\nLoss of receptor-mediated\nBAFF clearance\n→ BAFF rises further\nafter B-cell depletion"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     4. T-CELL HELP AND REGULATORY FAILURE  (ARM 2 ROOT)
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_tcell {
    label="4 · T세포 도움과 조절 실패 (T-cell Help & Regulatory Failure) — ARM 2의 뿌리";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#6A1B9A"; fillcolor="#F3E5F5"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#E1BEE7", color="#6A1B9A"];

    T_THYMUS  [label="흉선 출력\nThymic output (RTE, CD31+)\n— reduced in LOCID"];
    T_CD4N    [label="나이브 CD4\nNaive CD4 (CD45RA+CCR7+)\n<20% → LOCID phenotype"];
    T_CD4M    [label="기억/작동 CD4\nMemory-effector CD4"];
    T_TFH     [label="순환 Tfh\ncTfh (CXCR5+PD-1+)\nEXPANDED and Th1-SKEWED\nin dysregulated CVID"];
    T_ICOS    [label="ICOS / ICOSL\nGC entry and maintenance"];
    T_CD40L   [label="CD40L (CD154) → CD40\nthe canonical help signal\nfor CSR"];
    T_IL21    [label="IL-21\nTfh → B: plasma-cell\ndifferentiation, AID induction"];
    T_IL10    [label="IL-10\nregulatory; also plasma-cell\ndifferentiation"];
    T_TREG    [label="조절 T세포\nTreg (FOXP3+CD25hi)\nREDUCED number AND function\n— tracks autoimmunity"];
    T_CTLA4   [label="CTLA-4 표면 발현\nSurface CTLA-4 —\ntransendocytosis of\nCD80/CD86 from APC"];
    T_LRBAREC [label="LRBA-의존 CTLA-4 재순환\nLRBA-dependent CTLA-4\nrecycling from lysosome"];
    T_CD8ACT  [label="CD8 활성화\nHLA-DR+ CD38+ CD8\n— activation marker of\ndysregulation"];
    T_TEMRA   [label="TEMRA / 노화 T세포\nCD57+ senescent T,\ninverted CD4:CD8"];
    T_IFNG    [label="IFN-γ\nTh1 skew — the cytokine of\ngranuloma and GLILD"];
    T_IL6     [label="IL-6 / TNF-α\nsystemic inflammatory tone"];
    T_CXCL13  [label="CXCL13\nGC activity biomarker —\nelevated in GLILD"];
    T_LYMPHOP [label="T세포 림프페니아\nCD4 lymphopenia (LOCID)\n→ opportunistic infection\nrisk (PJP, CMV)"];
    T_ANERGY  [label="T세포 증식 반응 저하\nImpaired mitogen/antigen\nproliferation, reduced\nTCR repertoire diversity"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     5. INNATE IMMUNITY AND MICROBIAL TRANSLOCATION
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_innate {
    label="5 · 선천면역과 미생물 전위 (Innate Immunity & Microbial Translocation)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#EF6C00"; fillcolor="#FFF3E0"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=box, fillcolor="#FFE0B2", color="#EF6C00"];

    I_IGAMUC  [label="점막 IgA 부재\nAbsent secretory IgA\n★ NOT replaced by IVIG/SCIG\n— the structural gap in\nreplacement therapy"];
    I_BARRIER [label="장 점막 장벽\nGut mucosal barrier\nintegrity"];
    I_LPS     [label="미생물 전위\nMicrobial translocation\n— circulating LPS ↑"];
    I_SCD14   [label="sCD14 / LBP\nmonocyte activation marker,\ntracks translocation"];
    I_MONO    [label="단핵구 활성화\nActivated monocytes\n(CD16+, IL-12/IL-23)"];
    I_ISG     [label="I형 인터페론 서명\nType I IFN signature (ISG)\n— driven by translocation,\nnot by autoantibody"];
    I_TLR9    [label="TLR7/TLR9 저반응\nTLR9 hyporesponsiveness\nof CVID B cells"];
    I_PDC     [label="pDC 수 감소\nReduced plasmacytoid DC"];
    I_NK      [label="NK 세포\nNK number/function\n(EBV control)"];
    I_NEUT    [label="호중구\nNeutrophils — recruited\nto airway, effector of\nSTRUCTURAL damage"];
    I_COMP    [label="보체 옵소닌화\nComplement C3b/iC3b —\nrequires antibody to be\nefficiently fixed"];
    I_DYSBIO  [label="장내미생물 이상\nGut dysbiosis, reduced\ndiversity, Gammaproteobacteria\nexpansion"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     6. IMMUNOGLOBULIN REPLACEMENT PHARMACOKINETICS
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_igpk {
    label="6 · 면역글로불린 보충 PK (Immunoglobulin Replacement Pharmacokinetics)";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#0D47A1"; fillcolor="#E8EAF6"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=box, fillcolor="#C5CAE9", color="#0D47A1"];

    P_IVINF   [label="IVIG 정맥 주입\nIV infusion — 100% bioavailable,\nimmediate Cmax\n(q3-4 weeks)"];
    P_SCDEP   [label="피하 저장고\nSC depot — bioavailability\n~65% of IV, absorption\nhalf-life ~1-3 days"];
    P_HYAL    [label="재조합 히알루로니다제\nrHuPH20 — depolymerises\nhyaluronan → large-volume\nSC dispersion (fSCIG)"];
    P_LYMPH   [label="림프관 흡수\nLymphatic uptake\n— why SC absorption is slow\nand flat"];
    P_CENT    [label="중앙 구획 IgG\nPlasma IgG (central)\nVc ≈ 0.05-0.06 L/kg"];
    P_PERIPH  [label="말초/간질 IgG\nInterstitial IgG\n(≈ half of total body IgG)"];
    P_FCRN    [label="FcRn 재순환\nFcRn salvage in endothelium\nand monocytes → the reason\nIgG t½ is 3-4 weeks"];
    P_CATAB   [label="포화성 대사\nSaturable (FcRn-limited)\ncatabolism → nonlinear CL\nat very high dose"];
    P_HALF    [label="IgG 반감기\nt½ ≈ 30-40 d in PID\n(range 18-45 d; shorter with\nprotein loss or infection)"];
    P_SWING   [label="peak-trough 변동\nIVIG sawtooth: 600-800 mg/dL\nswing over 4 weeks\nvs flat weekly SCIG"];
    P_ADJ     [label="용량 보정 계수\nSC dose adjustment factor\n1.37 (EU, AUC-matched)\nto 1.53 (US label)"];
    P_LOSS    [label="비대사적 소실\nNon-catabolic loss:\nprotein-losing enteropathy,\nproteinuria, chylothorax,\nburns"];
    P_WT      [label="체중 기준 용량\nDosing on actual vs adjusted\nbody weight — matters in\nobesity (IgG is not\nfat-distributed)"];
    P_ENDOG   [label="잔존 내인성 IgG 생산\nResidual endogenous IgG\nfrom surviving long-lived\nplasma cells"];
    P_TOTAL   [label="측정되는 혈청 IgG\nMeasured serum IgG =\nexogenous + endogenous"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     7. FROM IgG CONCENTRATION TO ACTUAL PROTECTION
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_prot {
    label="7 · IgG 농도에서 실제 방어까지 (From Concentration to Protection) — trough는 대리지표일 뿐";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#00695C"; fillcolor="#E0F2F1"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=box, fillcolor="#B2DFDB", color="#00695C"];

    R_TROUGH  [label="IgG trough 농도\nSerum IgG trough (mg/dL)\n— the number everybody\ntitrates to"];
    R_SPECAB  [label="병원체 특이 옵소닌 항체\nPathogen-specific opsonic\nantibody titre\n— what actually protects"];
    R_BREADTH [label="공여자 풀 항체 폭\nDonor-pool breadth\n(≥1000 donors) — covers\ncommon serotypes well,\nrare ones poorly"];
    R_PNEUMO  [label="폐렴구균 혈청형 커버리지\nPneumococcal serotype\ncoverage in the pool\n(varies with donor\nvaccination era)"];
    R_HIB     [label="anti-Hib, anti-tetanus,\nanti-measles titres\n— the QC anchors of the pool"];
    R_OPSPH   [label="옵소닌 포식작용\nOpsonophagocytic killing\n(OPKA) — the functional assay"];
    R_AVID    [label="항체 결합력\nAvidity / affinity of\npooled IgG vs a matched\nnative response"];
    R_MUCGAP  [label="점막 방어 공백\nMucosal defence gap:\nserum IgG transudes poorly\nto airway surface,\nIgA absent entirely"];
    R_CELLIM  [label="세포성 면역\nT-cell-mediated immunity\n— untouched by replacement,\ncovers viruses and\nintracellular organisms"];
    R_BIOL    [label="개인별 생물학적 IgG 수준\n'Biologic IgG level' (Bonagura)\n— the trough at which THIS\npatient stops infecting;\nranges 500 → >1500"];
    R_VACC    [label="백신 반응\nVaccine response — impaired\nby definition; irrelevant\nonce on replacement\n(and unmeasurable)"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     8. PATHOGENS AND INFECTION EVENTS  (ARM 1 OUTPUT)
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_path {
    label="8 · 병원체와 감염 사건 (Pathogens & Infection Events) — ARM 1의 출력";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#C62828"; fillcolor="#FFEBEE"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=box, fillcolor="#FFCDD2", color="#C62828"];

    X_SPN     [label="Streptococcus pneumoniae\ncapsular polysaccharide —\nthe archetypal\nantibody-dependent organism"];
    X_HI      [label="Haemophilus influenzae\n(non-typeable) — the dominant\nchronic airway coloniser"];
    X_MCAT    [label="Moraxella catarrhalis,\nStaph. aureus"];
    X_MYCO    [label="Mycoplasma / Ureaplasma\n— septic arthritis, cystitis;\nneeds specific culture"];
    X_PSA     [label="Pseudomonas aeruginosa\n— acquired LATE, marks\nestablished bronchiectasis"];
    X_GIARD   [label="Giardia lamblia,\nCampylobacter jejuni,\nSalmonella — IgA-dependent\ngut defence"];
    X_NORO    [label="Chronic norovirus\n— villous atrophy mimicking\ncoeliac disease"];
    X_ENTERO  [label="Enterovirus\n(meningoencephalitis;\nclassically in\nagammaglobulinaemia)"];
    X_EBV     [label="EBV / CMV\n— lymphoproliferation and\nlymphoma driver"];
    X_PJP     [label="Pneumocystis jirovecii,\nfungal, mycobacterial\n— only when T-cell defect\nor immunosuppression"];
    X_COLON   [label="기도 집락화\nChronic airway colonisation\n(bacterial load in\nbronchial lumen)"];
    X_SINO    [label="상하기도 감염 사건\nSinopulmonary infection event\n(sinusitis, bronchitis, otitis)"];
    X_PNEU    [label="폐렴 사건\nPneumonia event\n★ the calibrated endpoint\nof the exposure-response"];
    X_INVAS   [label="침습 감염\nInvasive disease: bacteraemia,\nmeningitis, empyema"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     9. AIRWAY INFLAMMATION AND THE BRONCHIECTASIS RATCHET
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_airway {
    label="9 · 기도 염증과 기관지확장증 래칫 (Airway Inflammation & the Bronchiectasis Ratchet) — 비가역";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#B71C1C"; fillcolor="#FFF8F8"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=box, fillcolor="#FFCCBC", color="#BF360C"];

    W_IL8     [label="IL-8 / LTB4 / CXCL1\nneutrophil chemoattraction\nto the airway"];
    W_NE      [label="호중구 엘라스타제\nNeutrophil elastase +\nMMP-9 — the actual\nprotease that destroys\nairway wall"];
    W_AAT     [label="α1-antitrypsin / SLPI\nantiprotease shield\n(overwhelmed, not deficient)"];
    W_WALL    [label="기도벽 파괴\nAirway wall destruction:\nelastin, cartilage,\nsmooth muscle"];
    W_BE      [label="기관지확장증 범위\nBRONCHIECTASIS EXTENT\n★ IRREVERSIBLE STATE\n(Bhalla / modified Reiff\nHRCT score)", shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#FFAB91", color="#BF360C", penwidth=2.0];
    W_MUCUS   [label="점액 과분비 및 정체\nMucus hypersecretion and\nstasis in dilated airway"];
    W_MCC     [label="점액섬모 청소율 저하\nImpaired mucociliary\nclearance (secondary,\nstructural)"];
    W_TRAP    [label="공기 걸림 / 소기도 질환\nAir trapping, mosaic\nattenuation, obliterative\nbronchiolitis"];
    W_FEV1    [label="FEV1 (% 예측치)\nFEV1 % predicted —\nreversible + irreversible\ncomponents"];
    W_FEV1IRR [label="비가역 FEV1 손실\nIRREVERSIBLE FEV1 FLOOR\n— the ratchet's ledger", shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#FFAB91", color="#BF360C", penwidth=2.0];
    W_DLCO    [label="DLCO\ndiffusing capacity —\nfalls with GLILD more\nthan with bronchiectasis"];
    W_EXAC    [label="급성 악화\nExacerbation — the clinical\nunit of the ratchet"];
    W_HAEM    [label="객혈 / 만성 화농성 객담\nHaemoptysis, chronic\npurulent sputum"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     10. GLILD AND INTERSTITIAL LUNG DISEASE  (ARM 2)
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_glild {
    label="10 · GLILD / 간질성 폐질환 (Granulomatous-Lymphocytic ILD) — ARM 2, IgG 보충에 반응하지 않음";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#4A148C"; fillcolor="#F8F0FC"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=box, fillcolor="#E1BEE7", color="#4A148C"];

    L_LYMPHAGG [label="기관지 주위 림프 집합체\nPeribronchiolar lymphoid\naggregates, ectopic\ngerminal centres"];
    L_FOLLBR  [label="세기관지 여포염\nFollicular bronchiolitis"];
    L_LIP     [label="림프성 간질성 폐렴\nLymphoid interstitial\npneumonia (LIP)"];
    L_NSIP    [label="비특이 간질성 폐렴\nNSIP pattern,\norganising pneumonia"];
    L_GRAN    [label="비괴사성 육아종\nNon-caseating granuloma\n(lung, liver, spleen, skin)\n— sarcoid-like but distinct"];
    L_GLILD   [label="GLILD 활성도\nGLILD activity — composite\nof the four histologies;\n~10-20% of CVID,\nmortality-defining"];
    L_TH1     [label="Th1/IFN-γ 구동\nIFN-γ-driven macrophage\nactivation → granuloma"];
    L_FIBRO   [label="섬유아세포 활성화\nFibroblast activation,\nTGF-β, collagen deposition"];
    L_FIB     [label="간질 섬유화\nINTERSTITIAL FIBROSIS\n★ IRREVERSIBLE", shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#CE93D8", color="#4A148C", penwidth=2.0];
    L_REST    [label="제한성 환기장애\nRestrictive physiology:\nFVC ↓, TLC ↓, DLCO ↓↓"];
    L_PH      [label="폐고혈압\nPulmonary hypertension\n(late, prognosis-defining)"];
    L_HRCT    [label="HRCT 소견\nNodules, ground glass,\nreticulation, LAD;\nthe diagnostic substrate"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     11. POLYCLONAL LYMPHOPROLIFERATION AND LIVER
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_lproc {
    label="11 · 다클론성 림프증식과 간 (Polyclonal Lymphoproliferation & Liver) — ARM 2";
    style="filled,rounded"; color="#283593"; fillcolor="#E8EAF6"; fontsize=11;
    node [shape=box, fillcolor="#C5CAE9", color="#283593"];

    Y_LAD     [label="림프절 비대\nPersistent lymphadenopathy\n(polyclonal, reactive)"];
    Y_SPLEEN  [label="비장 비대\nSplenomegaly (~25-30%)\n— tracks CD21low B and\nCD8 activation"];
    Y_HYPERSP [label="비장 기능 과다\nHypersplenism →\nthrombocytopenia,\nneutropenia (mechanical,\nnot autoimmune)"];
    Y_NRH     [label="간 결절성 재생성 과증식\nNodular regenerative\nhyperplasia (NRH)"];
    Y_PORTAL  [label="비간경변성 문맥고혈압\nNon-cirrhotic portal\nhypertension → varices,\nascites"];
    Y_ALP     [label="담도 효소 상승\nCholestatic pattern:\nALP ↑, GGT ↑; may precede\nliver disease by years"];
    Y_SPLENEC [label="비장절제\nSplenectomy — historically\nfor refractory ITP", shape=hexagon, fillcolor="#FFCC80", color="#EF6C00"];
    Y_ASPLEN  [label="무비증 위험\nAsplenic encapsulated-organism\nrisk — MULTIPLICATIVE with\nabsent opsonising antibody", shape=octagon, fillcolor="#FFAB91", color="#BF360C"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     12. AUTOIMMUNE CYTOPENIAS AND OTHER AUTOIMMUNITY  (ARM 2)
